  "plan": "## Implementation Plan: Collapsible Details Pane\n\n### Overview\nAdd collapsible sections to the details pane in both TUI and web UI. Title and description always visible, history expanded by default, all other sections collapsed by default. Empty sections shown but collapsed.\n\n---\n\n### Phase 1: Web UI Implementation\n\n**File: `/home/paule/MAD/server/templates/client.html`**\n\n1. **Create collapsible section HTML structure**\n   - Use `<details>` and `<summary>` elements for native collapsible behavior\n   - Add CSS for styling: collapsed/expanded states, rotation indicators\n   - Create a helper function `createCollapsibleSection(title, content, isExpanded)` that returns HTML string\n\n2. **Modify `toggleFeatureDetail()` function (line 436)**\n   - Keep title, stage, board, created, ID as always-visible rows\n   - Always show description (uncollapsed)\n   - Wrap History in collapsible section - expanded by default\n   - Wrap Plan, Implementation Spec, Test Spec, Implementation Notes, Questions, Actions in collapsible sections - collapsed by default\n   - Handle empty sections: show collapsible section with empty content (collapsed)\n\n3. **Add CSS styles**\n   - Style `<details>` and `<summary>` for consistent look\n   - Add expand/collapse indicator (►/▼)\n   - Match existing dark theme colors\n\n---\n\n### Phase 2: TUI Implementation\n\n**File: `/home/paule/MAD/pipeline/tui.py`**\n\n1. **Add collapsible section support**\n   - Use Textual's `Collapsible` widget or create custom toggle behavior\n   - Modify `_feature_markdown()` to generate structured data instead of plain markdown\n   - Alternatively: keep markdown but add clickable section headers that toggle visibility\n\n2. **Track expansion state in UI**\n   - Add instance variables to track which sections are expanded (e.g., `_detail_expanded_sections: set`)\n   - Initialize with: title/description always visible, history expanded, others collapsed\n   - Default state: empty set (use defaults above)\n\n3. **Update detail view rendering**\n   - Modify `_feature_markdown()` or create new rendering method\n   - Use Textual's `Collapsible` widgets for each section\n   - Re-render on toggle without persisting state\n\n4. **Handle user interaction**\n   - Add keyboard shortcuts or click handlers to toggle sections\n   - Focus management for accessibility\n\n---\n\n### Phase 3: Shared Considerations\n\n1. **Empty section handling**\n   - Both UIs currently use `if feature.field:` to conditionally show sections\n   - Change to: always render section wrapper, but show \"(empty)\" or similar placeholder when content is empty\n   - Collapsed by default when empty\n\n2. **State management**\n   - No persistence needed - state resets on each details pane open\n   - TUI: use in-memory set/dict\n   - Web UI: use JavaScript variables (lost on page refresh)\n\n3. **Section order** (consistent across both UIs):\n   1. Title (always visible)\n   2. Description (always visible)\n   3. History (expanded default)\n   4. Plan (collapsed default)\n   5. Implementation Spec (collapsed default)\n   6. Test Spec (collapsed default)\n   7. Implementation Notes (collapsed default)\n   8. Questions for Human (collapsed default)\n   9. Pipeline Log (collapsed default) - TUI only\n\n---\n\n### Testing Checklist\n- [ ] Web UI: All sections render correctly\n- [ ] Web UI: Clicking section headers toggles visibility\n- [ ] Web UI: History expanded by default\n- [ ] Web UI: Empty sections show as collapsed\n- [ ] TUI: All sections render correctly\n- [ ] TUI: Toggle mechanism works (keyboard/click)\n- [ ] TUI: History expanded by default\n- [ ] TUI: Empty sections show as collapsed\n- [ ] Both UIs: State does not persist across sessions"
